// NINTH DROP, SAME MEMBERSHIP TEST, OPERATOR-ADMITTED (2026-09-29, relayed by proud-deer-538). One
// identity: whichever test.claim.live_deploy.emit claim first reads witness_approval_broker_dark_script_text
// is billed a marginal the generic bash emit path's per-step overhead causes (bundle lookup,
// grounding, translate, fidelity decode, token fold; jolly-bee-43's #12576 findings). Inherited
// from main and unchanged by gunbc#12482, which only re-planned the claim because
// deployment_spec_srv1 changed.
data floor_eval_step_cost_drop_dark_install_render_rows: List<EvalStepCostDropMeasurement> = [
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "test.claim.live_deploy.emit.the_receipt_command_substitutes_the_digest_rather_than_splicing_it" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "gunbc#12482 required floor run 36490489535 (job 109157637341), floor-shared-fill line for this identity: planned_as_changed_witness, verdict pass, marginal eval_steps over the new-witness budget with the script render's fill netted separately; the same marginal lands on whichever claim reads the script first (gunbc#12482 floor runs at e8d4fed9bd and c81cc22ff0 billed it to two other identities)" as NonEmptyStr,
  },
]

// TENTH DROP, SAME MEMBERSHIP TEST, OPERATOR-ADMITTED (eager-owl-205, 2026-09-30, on gunbc#12800,
// escalation msg_00eaf0e6). One identity: the ONLY claim that runs the real build-job producer,
// gunbc.fleet_converge_workflow fleet_converge_build_job_own_steps, to hold that the reset-observer
// dispatch admission is one of its steps. The admission step itself is cheap; the bill is the
// construction of the sibling release-bins steps, which the claim never inspects and which
// gunbc.fleet_workflow_steps builds whole whenever the list is demanded. The cost PREDATES
// gunbc#12800: it was paid before gunbc#12437 and first re-adjudicated when that change touched the
// claim. The step's content is held by its own claim under the budget, with no drop.
data floor_eval_step_cost_drop_build_job_membership_rows: List<EvalStepCostDropMeasurement> = [
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "test.claim.workflow_dispatch_input_witness.the_build_job_carries_the_reset_observer_dispatch_admission" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "PR required floor run 36765162766 of gunbc#12800 at 6cac35eb1a6, floor-shared-fill line for this identity: verdict pass, marginal_eval_steps=155333 with the shared fill netted separately, against the 72,300 new-witness budget. The same claim read marginal_eval_steps=174583 on run 36743802719 at ec1b8190320, when gunbc#12437's job-gate equality built the whole host-reset-return job inside it; splitting that equality into its own claim removed about 19k, so the ~155k is the cost the claim carried before gunbc#12437, not one this change introduced" as NonEmptyStr,
  },
]

// THE DAG EMIT ROUND TRIP (gunbc#12878; `gunbc.rung_drop`
// `dag_emit_round_trip_new_witness_eval_step_cost`). One identity: the only floor execution of the
// real ingest -> emit -> re-ingest path for the dag target. A round trip is two real parses by
// construction, and one parse of even this one-line module is about half the budget, so the bill
// is the parser's per-token cost paid twice, not the emit. Every other dag-emit claim supplies its
// input and measures under the budget (v2.test.execution.dag_emit_interface).
data floor_eval_step_cost_drop_dag_emit_round_trip_rows: List<EvalStepCostDropMeasurement> = [
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "v2.test.execution.dag_grammar_backward_round_trip.a_data_declaration_round_trips_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "gunbc#12878, required floor run 36844213690 (D0-ADJUDICATE BLOCKING line for this identity: verdict pass, over the new-witness budget), re-derived by claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/execution/dag_grammar_backward_round_trip_test.dag --function a_data_declaration_round_trips_holds. The billed work is two real parses (ingest and re-ingest) of a one-line data declaration" as NonEmptyStr,
  },
]

// THE dag TARGET TEXT ROUND-TRIP NESTED-BIND CLAIMS (gunbc#13233; `gunbc.rung_drop`
// `dag_text_round_trip_nested_bind_new_witness_eval_step_cost`). Two identities, each rendering one
// emitted two-Bind token sequence, lexing it and parsing it ONCE at `fn_body`. Two lets is the
// smallest text that exercises a Bind in the body block and a Bind in the value group, so the
// fragment cannot shrink without dropping the route. Their four one-let siblings in the same module
// measure under the budget on their own and are not here.
data floor_eval_step_cost_drop_dag_text_round_trip_rows: List<EvalStepCostDropMeasurement> = [
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "v2.test.emit.dag_target_text_round_trip.a_bind_with_a_bind_body_round_trips_as_text" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "gunbc#13233, PR required floor run 37210735827 at 9929145faf (main merged after gunbc#13244), D0-ADJUDICATE BLOCKING line for this identity: verdict pass, over the new-witness budget; re-derived by claim_batch --hermetic --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/emit/dag_target_text_round_trip_test.dag --function a_bind_with_a_bind_body_round_trips_as_text. The billed work is one render, one lex and one real parse at fn_body of a two-Bind text, and the parse carries most of it" as NonEmptyStr,
  },
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "v2.test.emit.dag_target_text_round_trip.a_bind_with_a_bind_value_round_trips_as_text" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "gunbc#13233, PR required floor run 37210735827 at 9929145faf (main merged after gunbc#13244), D0-ADJUDICATE BLOCKING line for this identity: verdict pass, over the new-witness budget; re-derived by claim_batch --hermetic --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/emit/dag_target_text_round_trip_test.dag --function a_bind_with_a_bind_value_round_trips_as_text. The billed work is one render, one lex and one real parse at fn_body of a two-Bind text, and the parse carries most of it" as NonEmptyStr,
  },
]

// THE FOREIGN-GRAMMAR EXTENDED-FUNCTION PARSE CLAIMS (v2.test.parse census phase 4; `gunbc.rung_drop`
// `foreign_grammar_extended_parse_new_witness_eval_step_cost`). Two identities, the kotlin and rust
// extended-function parses, each one tokenize and one real parse of a function exercising let/val, if,
// return and binary expressions through that language's grammar. Their grammar preparation is billed
// apart; the parse alone exceeds the budget.
data floor_eval_step_cost_drop_foreign_grammar_extended_parse_rows: List<EvalStepCostDropMeasurement> = [
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "test.claim.parse_test_kotlin_grammar.claim_kotlin_extended_function_parses_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "v2.test.parse census phase 4, claim_batch BuildBuddy invocations 2c8f9d0b and 9241511f on main of 2026-10-05 plus this change: verdict pass, the claim's own marginal over the new-witness budget even with its grammar preparation billed apart; re-derived by claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/parse/parse_test_kotlin_grammar_test.dag --functions claim_kotlin_extended_function_parses_holds. The billed work is one tokenize and one real parse of an extended function with the language's own grammar" as NonEmptyStr,
  },
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "test.claim.parse_test_rust_grammar.claim_rust_extended_function_parses_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "v2.test.parse census phase 4, claim_batch BuildBuddy invocations 2c8f9d0b and 9241511f on main of 2026-10-05 plus this change: verdict pass, the claim's own marginal over the new-witness budget even with its grammar preparation billed apart; re-derived by claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/parse/parse_test_rust_grammar_test.dag --functions claim_rust_extended_function_parses_holds. The billed work is one tokenize and one real parse of an extended function with the language's own grammar" as NonEmptyStr,
    },
  ]

// THE COPRODUCT FRAGMENT-LOWERING CLAIMS (v2.test.parse census phase 3; `gunbc.rung_drop`
// `coproduct_fragment_normalize_new_witness_eval_step_cost`). Three identities, each parsing ONE type
// declaration fragment at its production and lowering it with normalize_node (two, for the two
// equality claims). The fragment is the smallest text carrying the construct each claim names, so it
// cannot shrink without dropping the route. The module's other claims measure under the budget and are
// not here; its four fn-fragment claims exceed the CPU enrolment margin and are not gated at all.
data floor_eval_step_cost_drop_coproduct_fragment_normalize_rows: List<EvalStepCostDropMeasurement> = [
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
    identity: "test.claim.parse_test_coproduct_leading_pipe.positional_payload_variants_parse_and_normalize_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
    measured_by: "v2.test.parse census phase 3, claim_batch BuildBuddy invocation acf43cce at main plus gunbc#13410 plus this change: verdict pass, over the new-witness budget; re-derived by claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/parse/parse_test_coproduct_leading_pipe_test.dag --functions positional_payload_variants_parse_and_normalize_holds. The billed work is one real parse of one declaration fragment at its production and its lowering by normalize_node; the scaling is read in BuildBuddy invocations d04df9ae and b01c394f" as NonEmptyStr,
  },
  EvalStepCostDropMeasurement {
